{"seq":29,"data":{"type":"RUN_FINISHED","threadId":"94b65481-dcca-4727-bd08-5cc65473d4e9","runId":"run_1_1788367218001","result":"Perfect! I've created the regex and saved it to `/app/regex.txt`.\n\nHere's how the regex works:\n\n**Key Components:**\n\n1. **IPv4 Address Detection** - `(?=.*\\b(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4]\\d|1\\d{2}|[1-9]?\\d)\\.(...)\\b)`\n   - Lookahead ensures the line contains a valid IPv4 address\n   - Each octet pattern matches 0-255 without leading zeros\n\n2. **Greedy Match to Last Date** - `.*`\n   - Greedily matches everything, forcing the regex to find the rightmost valid date\n\n3. **Date Pattern with Month/Day Constraints**:\n   - **31-day months** (01,03,05,07,08,10,12): `(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])`\n   - **30-day months** (04,06,09,11): `(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|30)`\n   - **February** (up to 29 days): `02-(?:0[1-9]|1\\d|2[0-9])`\n\n4. **Word Boundaries** - `(?<![A-Za-z0-9-])` and `(?![A-Za-z0-9-])`\n   - Prevents false matches like \"1134-12-1234\" or \"text2024-01-15text\"\n\nWhen used with `re.findall()` and `re.MULTILINE`, this will extract only the last valid date from each line that contains an IPv4 address.","rawEvent":{"duration_api_ms":102652,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"94b65481-dcca-4727-bd08-5cc65473d4e9","total_cost_usd":0.09805460000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":17,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15226,"cache_read_input_tokens":26321,"output_tokens":15025,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":14202},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15226},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":8,"output_tokens":817,"cache_read_input_tokens":13632,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14283,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14283,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens